<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth rises to 15.7 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth rises to 15.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth edged up to 15.7 percent on October 11 from 15.3 percent on September 27, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Oct 11, 1996   Sept 27, 1996  Oct 13, 1995</p>
<p>		   15.7		15.3	     14.94</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,438.27 billion rupees on October 11 compared to 6,394.14 billion rupees on September 27, 1996 and 5,549.24 billion on October 13, 1995, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
